# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<template>
  <p>{{ total() }}</p>
  <button @click="total()">Log</button>
  <p v-if="label()">{{ label }}</p>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: { title: String },
  computed: {
    total() {
      return 42;
    },
    label() {
      return this.title;
    },
  },
};
</script>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-template.vue:3:9 lint/nursery/noVueComputedPropertyCall ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The computed property total is called like a method, but its value is not a function.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
    2 │ <template>
  > 3 │   <p>{{ total() }}</p>
      │         ^^^^^^^
    4 │   <button @click="total()">Log</button>
    5 │   <p v-if="label()">{{ label }}</p>
  
  i Vue gives you the value that the getter of a computed property returns. Calling a value that is not a function throws an error when the code runs.
  
  i Remove the parentheses and the arguments to read the value of the computed property.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

